# Copy to local.env and fill in. Gitignored.
#
# MAGNET_BUNDLE_ID     reverse-DNS id for your build. This is also the UserDefaults
#                     domain and the prefix for Keychain service names, so pick one
#                     and keep it -- changing it later orphans your settings.
# MAGNET_SIGN_IDENTITY name of a self-signed code-signing certificate, created
#                     automatically on first build. Keeping it stable is what stops
#                     macOS re-asking for permissions after every rebuild.
# MAGNET_HTTP_HOSTS    comma-separated hosts you reach over plain HTTP (a LAN or
#                     tailnet address for qBittorrent, say, or the NAS running
#                     nas/automatic). Each gets an App Transport Security exception.
#                     Leave empty if everything is HTTPS.
# MAGNET_NAS_SSH       user@host that nas/automatic/deploy.sh copies the Automatic
#                     service to. Only needed for Automatic mode.
# MAGNET_NAS_DIR       the folder on that host it is deployed into.
: "${MAGNET_BUNDLE_ID:=com.example.magnet}"
: "${MAGNET_SIGN_IDENTITY:=Magnet Local Signing}"
: "${MAGNET_HTTP_HOSTS:=}"
: "${MAGNET_NAS_SSH:=}"
: "${MAGNET_NAS_DIR:=}"
